{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the cause and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200 (\"Submission received\", stage \"mitigation\"). The submit command ran right after a check that showed no frontend errors in the previous 20 seconds. I haven't seen end-user traffic since the fix, so I don't know yet whether the grader's sustained-period check passes.\n\n**Root cause:** the PostgreSQL role `otelu` had a password that didn't match the one stored in the `product-catalog-db-conn` secret and the `product-reviews` deployment. Both services were failing with `password authentication failed for user \"otelu\"`. That made the frontend return \"Product Not Found\" and checkout fail.\n\n**Fix:** I reset the `otelu` password in PostgreSQL to the value both services already use. I then confirmed that `otelu` can read `catalog.products` and `reviews.productreviews`, and restarted `product-catalog`. I didn't change any Kubernetes config or secrets."}}
